{"term":"regret","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:3d76499f61a2032cae","definition":"To feel sorry about (a thing that has or has not happened), afterthink: to wish that a thing had not happened, that something else had happened instead.","example":"He regretted his words.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["rue"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["live to regret","regrettable","regretter","regrettingly","unregretted","unregretting"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regret#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1b8876844159d43ac2","definition":"To feel sorry about (any thing).","example":"I regret that I have to do this, but I don't have a choice.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["grieve","lament","aggrieve","besorrow","condole","darken","engrieve","erme","gloom","grieve","grieven","bleed","lament","moan","mourn","remorse","repent","regret","rue","sigh","sorrow","wayment","yearn"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"broadly","register":"broadly","wordFamily":["live to regret","regrettable","regretter","regrettingly","unregretted","unregretting"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regret#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e56dd8491ef1a14df8","definition":"To miss; to feel the loss or absence of; to mourn.","example":"He more than ever regretted his home, and with increased desire longed to see his family.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, transitive","wordFamily":["live to regret","regrettable","regretter","regrettingly","unregretted","unregretting"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regret#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0f252358d176ac5d2c","d